<title>HONG KONG: Hong Kong July air cargo by country.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong July air cargo by country.</headline>
<byline>Jim Gilchrist</byline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong civil aviation department statistics show total air cargo handled in July by country rose by 1.6 per cent compared with the same month last year. Air cargo imports on both scheduled and non-scheduled flights reached 62,714 tonnes and 68,328 tonnes for exports.</p>
<p>The top 15 countries figures (rounded) are shown in tonnes in the table below in alphabetical order.</p>
<p>				 JULY 1996 All cargo</p>
<p>			Unloaded     Loaded	 Pct change from</p>
<p>							  July 1995 for all</p>
<p>							  cargo</p>
<p>Australia	   2,742.4	 2,552.8     -4.9</p>
<p>Canada		2,005.4	 1,557.5     54.2</p>
<p>China Mainland    1,724.5	 2,892.1	5.32</p>
<p>France		2,206.4	 1,897.0	2.3</p>
<p>Germany	     3,759.3	 3,717.2	0.1</p>
<p>Japan		 5,931.5	11,272.3     -6.8</p>
<p>South Korea	 3,106.7	 3,984.7	4.3</p>
<p>Malaysia	    1,855.3	 1,490.5     -6.2</p>
<p>Netherlands	 1,169.1	 1,056.0    -11.6</p>
<p>Philippines	 1,623.4	 1,794.1     -2.72</p>
